│ but not at the time of the survey), or never users. Results.—In 162,576 participants, the prevalence of migraine was │
│ 17.1% in women and 5.6% in men. Only 56.2% of those with migraine had ever received a medical diagnosis.             │
│ Ninety‐eight percent of the migraineurs used acute treatment for their migraine attacks. Forty‐nine percent (49%)    │
